---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sessions = (await getCollection('sessions')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.date.valueOf() - b.data.date.valueOf()
);
const latest = sessions[sessions.length - 1];
const fmt = (d: Date) => d.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---
<Layout title="Story So Far">
  <p class="eyebrow">A Dungeons &amp; Dragons Chronicle</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Out of the Abyss</h1>
  <p class="lead">A drow prison, a handful of captives, and the long climb out of the dark. This is the chronicle of our campaign — the story so far, session by session.</p>

  <img class="story-hero" src="/images/sessions/vrock-and-ooze.png" alt="The party on the shore of the pool, an ooze rising behind them and a vulture-demon looming" />

  <section class="prose" style="margin-top:40px">
    <h2>The Story So Far</h2>

    <p>
      It began in chains. Five strangers — the elf warlock <strong>Ilyrion Silverstar</strong>, the dwarf
      cleric <strong>Jebediah Brightstone</strong>, the human rogue <strong>Kit</strong>, the elf rogue
      <strong>Rhys Toromakian</strong>, and the human fighter <strong>Thibaud</strong> — woke as prisoners
      of the drow, stripped of everything and thrown into the slave pen of <strong>Velkynvelve</strong>.
      Around them languished ten other captives, all of them waiting for a slaver's party from
      Menzoberranzan that was already days overdue.
    </p>

    <img class="float-right" src="/images/velkynvelve/ilvara-mizzrym.png" alt="Ilvara, commander of Velkynvelve" />

    <p>
      The outpost's commander, the priestess <strong>Ilvara</strong>, ruled by cruelty. When the party
      goaded the bully <strong>Ront</strong> into snapping his chains, the guards struck him down and Ilvara
      had him fed to the giant spiders below — a lesson written in blood. Yet even here the prisoners found
      one another: the party saved the gentle myconid <strong>Stool</strong> from Ront's torment, and in
      gratitude he gave them a priceless gift — spores that let them all speak mind to mind.
    </p>

    <p>
      Through whispered, telepathic talk they gathered allies and secrets. The deep gnome spy
      <strong>Jimjar</strong> revealed a rift among the drow leaders. The serene kuo-toa
      <strong>Shuushar</strong> spoke of escaping madness through peace. The dwarf <strong>Eldeth</strong>
      placed her trust — and a dying request — in Ilyrion's hands. And the quaggoth
      <strong>Derendil</strong> swore he was a cursed elven prince.
    </p>

    <img class="float-left" src="/images/velkynvelve/eldeth.png" alt="Eldeth Feldrun, the dwarf prisoner" />

    <p>
      Then the dark turned darker. Three of the party were visited by nightmares of groping shadows and
      buzzing madness, waking certain that something <em>worse than the drow</em> stirred in the deep. By
      morning <strong>Eldeth lay murdered</strong>, her body posed as a sacrifice to a god of murder. With
      the slavers' arrival looming, the party struck a desperate bargain with the disgraced warrior
      <strong>Jorlan</strong>: he would leave the gate open and raise a distraction — and they would make
      sure the blame fell on his rival.
    </p>

    <img class="float-right clear" src="/images/players/joy.png" alt="Joy, the elf prisoner" />

    <p>
      The plan held. On the morning of the break-out a sixth captive was thrown in among them — the
      elf <strong>Joy</strong>, her ears cut away, lately the property of a circus — and then Jorlan
      opened the gate and disappeared. Judging the armoury not worth their lives, the party left
      their equipment where it lay, cut down through the giant spiders' webs and swam a pool that
      spoke into their minds: <em>flesh for the faceless lord</em>.
    </p>

    <p>
      They surfaced into chaos. Demons came howling out of the north passage and fell on
      <strong>Velkynvelve</strong>, and under cover of the slaughter the prisoners ran for the west
      tunnel — until a dying, vulture-like demon crashed down across it, and a shackled deep gnome
      named <strong>Jimjar</strong> tore its jaws apart with his bare hands.
    </p>

    <p>
      Now they are loose in the Underdark with no gear, no boots and no map, an enraged
      <strong>Ilvara</strong> hunting them with her commanders, and a week of tunnels between them
      and <strong>Sloobludop</strong> on the shores of the Darklake. They have bought water and
      rations from a duergar trader with a gemstone and a lie — and something worse than the drow is
      still waiting further down.
    </p>

    {latest && (
      <p>
        <a href={`/sessions/${latest.slug}`}>→ Read the latest session: <em>{latest.data.title}</em> ({fmt(latest.data.date)})</a>
      </p>
    )}
  </section>
</Layout>
